\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces Best and worst individual ticker fits under the sector-specific NN calibration, ranked by RMSE across all 31 tickers. The best fits were dominated by the broad-market ETFs and the deep-liquidity financials (GS, JPM); the worst fits were concentrated in technology (QCOM, MU, INTC, AMD) and healthcare (PFE, MRNA), where within-sector smile heterogeneity was largest. PFE and BMY remained the only tickers below the 2{,}000-observation per-ticker threshold.}}{37}{table.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:worst_tickers}{{S3}{37}{Best and worst individual ticker fits under the sector-specific NN calibration, ranked by RMSE across all 31 tickers. The best fits were dominated by the broad-market ETFs and the deep-liquidity financials (GS, JPM); the worst fits were concentrated in technology (QCOM, MU, INTC, AMD) and healthcare (PFE, MRNA), where within-sector smile heterogeneity was largest. PFE and BMY remained the only tickers below the 2{,}000-observation per-ticker threshold}{table.caption.13}{}}
